    family's glass; an original wallpaper; the default layout's Look and Feel.
  * The fonts: the look names Charcoal, Geneva and Monaco and uses them where installed; fontconfig aliases give the
    free fonts measured nearest to them (Noto Sans Display, DejaVu Sans, Inconsolata). None of the classic fonts ships.
  * kubabbar-glass-9-sync brings the Kvantum theme and the fonts into the session through the look's own defaults
    store, so a person's own fonts and Kvantum choice are never overwritten (Plasma's Look and Feel manager removes a
    person's own value of each key it applies); it removes exactly what it wrote when another look is applied.
  * Every text reads at 4.5:1 or more: the schemes on their own backgrounds, the Plasma style's over its translucent
    surfaces on the wallpaper (Daniel, 2026-11-25: "yes, fix them. bring them to a readable level").
  * Depends on the edition's Kvantum (kvantum 1.1.8-1+stereo3d1), which knows the scroll_arrows_together key.

